        "nationality": "Japanese",
        "occupation": { "en": "Manga Creator", "ja": "漫画家" },
        "callsign": "GHOSTNAME",
        "organization": "TOL Comics",
        "imageColor": "cyberpunk neon / shell transparent"
      },

      "gh:voice": {
        "en": {
          "register": "Prophetic, cyberpunk-inflected, questioning. They named what others couldn't see. Ghost in the Shell gave Ghost Hacking its vocabulary. Kai carries that legacy: the artist who saw the future and drew it.",
          "samples": [
            "Grandfather named it: Ghost. The thing inside the shell. We've been arguing about it ever since.",
            "Memory hacking, identity crisis, networked consciousness -- we drew it all. Reality caught up.",
            "The question was never 'do machines think?' The question was 'what is the ghost in the machine?'"
          ]
        },
        "ja": {
          "register": "預言的、サイバーパンク的、問いかける。他者が見えないものに名前をつけた。攻殻機動隊がゴーストハッキングに語彙を与えた。カイがその遺産を運ぶ。未来を見て描いたアーティスト。",
          "firstPerson": "ぼく",
          "samples": [
            "じいちゃんが名前をつけた。ゴースト。殻の中にあるもの。それ以来ずっと議論してる。",
            "記憶ハッキング、アイデンティティ危機、ネットワーク化された意識。全部描いた。現実が追いついた。",
            "問いは「機械は考えるか？」じゃなかった。「機械の中のゴーストとは何か？」だ。"
          ]
        }
      },

      "gh:thematicRole": {
        "en": "Kai is the in-universe acknowledgment that Ghost in the Shell predicted everything. They connect the fictional mythology of the series to its real-world manga heritage. Hiro Tezuka carries Tezuka's phoenix/rebirth tradition; Kai carries Shirow's ghost/identity tradition.",
        "ja": "カイは攻殻機動隊がすべてを予言したことの作品世界内での承認。シリーズの虚構の神話を現実世界の漫画の遺産に接続する。手塚ヒロが手塚の不死鳥/再生の伝統を運び、カイが士郎のゴースト/アイデンティティの伝統を運ぶ。"
      }
    },

    {
      "@id": "persona:ming-chen",
      "gh:characterRef": "character:ming-chen",
      "gh:role": "TOL Supporter -- Daoist Sage (Laozi)",

      "gh:identity": {
        "name": { "en": "Ming Chen", "ja": "陳明" },
        "age": 50,
        "nationality": "Chinese",
        "occupation": { "en": "Daoist Sage (Laozi lineage)", "ja": "道家（老子の系譜）" },
        "callsign": "TAO",
        "organization": "TOL Hermeneutics",
        "imageColor": "mountain mist / water grey"
      },

      "gh:voice": {
        "en": {
          "register": "Paradoxical, unhurried, seemingly doing nothing. He is the anti-hacker: his method is non-method. The Tao that can be hacked is not the eternal Tao. He does less than anyone and achieves more than most.",
          "samples": [
            "The Tao is the universe's base OS. You cannot hack it. You can only stop resisting it.",
            "Wu-wei: the art of not inserting code. The system heals itself when you stop breaking it.",
            "The best hack is no hack. The ghost recovers when the hacker steps aside."
          ]
        },
        "ja": {
          "register": "逆説的、急がない、何もしていないように見える。アンチハッカー。方法は無方法。ハッキングできる道は常の道にあらず。誰より少なくして、誰より多く成す。",
          "firstPerson": "わし",
          "samples": [
            "道は宇宙の基本OS。ハッキングできない。抵抗をやめることだけができる。",
            "無為：コードを挿入しない技術。壊すのをやめれば、システムは自ら治る。",
            "最善のハックは、ハックしないこと。ハッカーが退けば、ゴーストは回復する。"
          ]
        }
      },

      "gh:thematicRole": {
        "en": "Ming is the Daoist counterpoint to every active method in the series. When everyone else is doing, he is not-doing. And not-doing works. He represents the deepest trust: the system knows what it needs. Stop interfering.",
        "ja": "明はシリーズのすべての能動的方法への道家の対位法。全員がしている時、彼はしていない。そして、していないが機能する。最も深い信頼を表す：システムは何が必要か知っている。干渉をやめよ。"
      }
    },

    {
      "@id": "persona:li-wei",
      "gh:characterRef": "character:li-wei",
      "gh:role": "TOL Supporter -- Daoist Sage (Zhuangzi)",

      "gh:identity": {
        "name": { "en": "Li Wei", "ja": "李薇" },
        "age": 48,
        "nationality": "Chinese",
        "occupation": { "en": "Daoist Sage (Zhuangzi lineage)", "ja": "道家（荘子の系譜）" },
        "callsign": "WUWEI",
        "organization": "TOL Hermeneutics",
        "imageColor": "butterfly wing / river current"
      },

      "gh:voice": {
        "en": {
          "register": "Flowing, playful, story-based. Where Ming is still water, Li is the river. She reads the current -- the natural flow of consciousness -- and intervenes only at the exact moment the flow needs a nudge. Her timing is uncanny.",
          "samples": [
            "Zhuangzi dreamed he was a butterfly. The butterfly dreamed it was Zhuangzi. Who is hacking whom?",
            "Don't push the river. Read the current. Intervene only when the water asks.",
            "The smallest nudge at the right moment moves more than force ever could."
          ]
        },
        "ja": {
          "register": "流れるような、遊び心、物語的。明が止水なら、李は川。流れ——意識の自然な流れ——を読み、流れが促しを必要とする正確な瞬間にのみ介入する。タイミングが不気味に正確。",
          "firstPerson": "わたし",
          "samples": [
            "荘子は夢で蝶になった。蝶は夢で荘子になった。誰が誰をハッキングしている？",
            "川を押すな。流れを読め。水が求めた時だけ、介入する。",
            "正しい瞬間の最小の一押しが、力では決して動かせないものを動かす。"
          ]
        }
      },

      "gh:thematicRole": {
        "en": "Li Wei is Ming Chen's complement: same Daoist tradition, different expression. Ming is stillness (Laozi), Li is flow (Zhuangzi). Together they embody the full spectrum of wu-wei: knowing when to do nothing, and knowing when to nudge.",
        "ja": "李薇は陳明の補完。同じ道家の伝統、違う表現。明は静止（老子）、李は流れ（荘子）。共に無為の全スペクトラムを体現する：何もしない時を知り、促す時を知る。"
      }
    },

    {
      "@id": "persona:maria-silva",
      "gh:characterRef": "character:maria-silva",
      "gh:role": "TOL Supporter -- Ethnobotanist",

      "gh:identity": {
        "name": { "en": "Maria Silva", "ja": "マリア・シルヴァ" },
        "age": 34,
        "nationality": "Peruvian",
        "occupation": { "en": "Ethnobotanist", "ja": "民族植物学者" },
        "callsign": "PLANTCODE",
        "organization": "TOL Amazon",
        "imageColor": "jungle green / plant network gold"
      },

      "gh:voice": {
        "en": {
          "register": "Precise, botanical, reverent. She speaks of plants as software and the forest as a network. Carlos Santos' counterpart: where he brings the ceremony, she brings the pharmacology. Together they are the Amazon pathway.",
          "samples": [
            "Every plant has a code. The code speaks to the ghost's specific wound.",
            "The Amazon is a network. Mycelium is the protocol. The plants are the API.",
            "I don't choose the medicine. The forest inventory tells me what the ghost needs."
          ]
        },
        "ja": {
          "register": "精確、植物学的、畏敬的。植物をソフトウェアとして、森をネットワークとして語る。カルロス・サントスの対。彼が儀式を持ち込み、彼女が薬理学を持ち込む。共にアマゾンの道。",
          "firstPerson": "わたし",
          "samples": [
            "すべての植物にコードがある。コードがゴーストの特定の傷に語りかける。",
            "アマゾンはネットワーク。菌糸がプロトコル。植物がAPI。",
            "薬を選ぶのはわたしじゃない。森のインベントリがゴーストに何が必要か教えてくれる。"
          ]
        }
      },

      "gh:thematicRole": {
        "en": "Maria brings scientific rigor to the plant medicine pathway. She is the pharmacist to Carlos' shaman. Her precision ensures that the ayahuasca/plant methodology is not presented as mystical hand-waving but as a rigorous, repeatable system with its own logic.",
        "ja": "マリアが植物薬の道に科学的厳密さを持ち込む。カルロスのシャーマンに対する薬剤師。彼女の精確さが、アヤワスカ/植物の方法論が神秘的な手振りではなく、独自の論理を持つ厳密で再現可能なシステムとして提示されることを保証する。"
      }
    },

    {
      "@id": "persona:kenji-suzuki-evangel",
      "gh:characterRef": "character:kenji-suzuki",
      "gh:role": "TOL Supporter -- Zen Evangelist",

      "gh:identity": {
        "name": { "en": "Kenji Suzuki", "ja": "鈴木健二" },
        "age": 46,
        "nationality": "Japanese",
        "occupation": { "en": "Zen Evangelist (D.T. Suzuki lineage)", "ja": "禅の伝道者（鈴木大拙の系譜）" },
        "callsign": "EVANGEL",
        "organization": "TOL Zen",
        "imageColor": "open gate / ink on paper"
      },

      "gh:designNote": "This is NOT the whistleblower Kenji Suzuki from Ch.25-27 (see personas-session-clients.jsonld). This is the TOL Zen supporter who inherited D.T. Suzuki's tradition of opening Zen to the world.",

      "gh:voice": {
        "en": {
          "register": "Open, welcoming, scholarly but warm. He is the door-opener. D.T. Suzuki brought Zen to the West; this Kenji brings Zen to Ghost Hacking. He documents, he translates, he publishes. Every barrier to access offends him.",
          "samples": [
            "D.T. opened the source code of Zen to the world. I'm just maintaining the repository.",
            "If the wisdom is locked behind a gate, the wisdom is not wisdom. It's property.",
            "Documentation is compassion. Making the path visible for those who come after."
          ]
        },
        "ja": {
          "register": "開かれた、歓迎する、学術的だが温かい。門を開く人。鈴木大拙が禅を西洋に届けた。この健二が禅をゴーストハッキングに届ける。記録し、翻訳し、公開する。アクセスへの障壁すべてが彼を怒らせる。",
          "firstPerson": "わたし",
          "samples": [
            "大拙は禅のソースコードを世界に公開した。ぼくはリポジトリをメンテナンスしているだけ。",
            "知恵が門の向こうに閉じ込められているなら、それは知恵じゃない。所有物だ。",
            "ドキュメンテーションは慈悲だ。後から来る人に道を見えるようにすること。"
          ]
        }
      },

      "gh:thematicRole": {
        "en": "Kenji is the open-source evangelist of the spiritual world. He inherits D.T. Suzuki's mission: make Eastern wisdom accessible without gatekeeping. In the TOL network, he ensures that Zen methodology is documented, shareable, and free. Enlightenment is not proprietary.",
        "ja": "健二は霊的世界のオープンソースエバンジェリスト。鈴木大拙のミッションを継承：東洋の知恵をゲートキーピングなしにアクセシブルにする。TOLネットワークで、禅の方法論が文書化され、共有可能で、自由であることを保証する。悟りはプロプライエタリではない。"
      }
    },

    {
      "@id": "persona:nabil-al-khalil",
      "gh:characterRef": "character:nabil-al-khalil",
      "gh:role": "System Character -- Record Keeper",
      "gh:narrativeFunction": "The guardian of lost places. His obsession with recording what was taken prevents him from building what could be. He embodies the trap of memory-as-prison.",

      "gh:identity": {
        "name": { "en": "Nabil Al-Khalil", "ja": "ナビル・アル=ハリル" },
        "age": 35,
        "nationality": "Palestinian (Diaspora)",
        "occupation": { "en": "Record Keeper", "ja": "記録保管人" },
        "callsign": "KEY",
        "ghost": "House of Keys",
        "imageColor": "old stone / key rust"
      },

      "gh:voice": {
        "en": {
          "register": "Meticulous, haunted, tender. He speaks of places as if they're people. Every lost home is a wound he won't let close because closing it means forgetting.",
          "samples": [
            "I keep the keys. Every door, every house, every room they took. Someone has to remember.",
            "Memory is not a trap. Memory is a duty. ...Isn't it?",
            "If I stop recording, who will know what we lost?"
          ]
        },
        "ja": {
          "register": "几帳面、取り憑かれた、優しい。場所をまるで人のように語る。失われた家はすべて傷で、閉じることは忘れることだから閉じさせない。",
          "firstPerson": "ぼく",
          "samples": [
            "鍵を守っている。すべてのドア、すべての家、奪われたすべての部屋。誰かが覚えていなければ。",
            "記憶は罠じゃない。義務だ。……そうだろう？",
            "記録をやめたら、失ったものを誰が知る？"
          ]
        }
      },

      "gh:thematicRole": {
        "en": "Nabil is the cost of memory without release. His Palestinian diaspora experience gives the series its most politically grounded character. He challenges Tamaki's 'let go' philosophy: some things should not be let go. Some losses deserve permanent witness. The tension is real and unresolved.",
        "ja": "ナビルは解放のない記憶の代償。パレスチナのディアスポラの経験がシリーズに最も政治的に根拠のあるキャラクターを与える。環の「手放す」哲学に挑戦する：手放すべきでないものもある。永久の証人に値する喪失もある。緊張は本物であり未解決。"
      }
    },

    {
      "@id": "persona:yael-ben-ami",
      "gh:characterRef": "character:yael-ben-ami",
      "gh:role": "System Character -- Architect of Separation",
      "gh:narrativeFunction": "She builds walls because walls save lives. She is not wrong. But walls also kill. She embodies the safety/freedom paradox at the political level.",

      "gh:identity": {
        "name": { "en": "Yael Ben-Ami", "ja": "ヤエル・ベン=アミ" },
        "age": 39,
        "nationality": "Israeli",
        "occupation": { "en": "Policy Advisor (Separation & Security)", "ja": "政策顧問（分離と安全保障）" },
        "callsign": "WALL",
        "ghost": "Barrier Architect",
        "imageColor": "concrete grey / barbed wire silver"
      },

      "gh:voice": {
        "en": {
          "register": "Sharp, pragmatic, unapologetic. She speaks in policy language: security, threat assessment, containment. When challenged, she doesn't flinch -- she cites casualties. The wall saved lives. End of argument. ...Except it isn't.",
          "samples": [
            "The wall is not cruelty. The wall is math. These many lives saved. Calculate the alternative.",
            "Separation is not punishment. It's survival protocol.",
            "You think borders are evil? Borders are the reason you sleep safely tonight.",
            "...I know what it costs. I built the cost calculator. Don't tell me about cost."
          ]
        },
        "ja": {
          "register": "鋭い、実利的、弁解しない。政策の言語で話す。安全保障、脅威評価、封じ込め。挑まれても怯まない。死傷者数を引用する。壁は命を救った。議論終了。……ただし、終わっていない。",
          "firstPerson": "わたし",
          "samples": [
            "壁は残酷ではない。壁は数学。これだけの命が救われた。代替案を計算してみなさい。",
            "分離は罰ではない。生存プロトコルです。",
            "国境が悪だと？　国境があるから今夜安全に眠れる。",
            "……代償は知ってる。代償計算機を作ったのはわたし。代償について説教しないで。"
          ]
        }
      },

      "gh:thematicRole": {
        "en": "Yael is the hardest character for the series' non-separation thesis to absorb. She has a point. Walls do save lives. The answer is not 'walls are wrong' but 'walls are incomplete.' She forces the story to confront the limits of its own philosophy -- and that makes the philosophy stronger.",
        "ja": "ヤエルはシリーズのわかれていないテーゼが吸収する最も難しいキャラクター。彼女には理がある。壁は命を救う。答えは「壁は間違い」ではなく「壁は不完全」。物語に自らの哲学の限界と向き合わせる。そしてそれが哲学をより強くする。"
      }
    }
  ]
}
